Subject: Admit the original SuperLoadingScene and FE-to-game loading start
Upstream-base: efa6fc84680e48bfdca7e6ac245d8abf333ae617
Classification: temporary explicit original-source diagnostic admission; depends on 0551-0555 and 0600.

Stadium Select's PLAY NOW and tournament Choose Sides' Proceed call
PushLoadingScene(true), which pushes SCENE_SUPER_LOADING (SuperLoadingScene,
TT_3D_TRANSITION). Its SceneCreated runs the authored match sequence (VM
instruction 19, the fixed 0xB60A9CC0 FE audio event, is admitted with the
briefing gate) and its Update requests task state 0x200000 once the
presentation is idle; the original LoadingTask::StateTransition(4, 0x200000)
then starts the FELoadingToGame async loading sequence.

Under the named MSCHARGED_DIAGNOSTIC_FRONTEND_MATCH_LOADING admission, move
factory case SCENE_SUPER_LOADING (not the cross-fader, 16), VM instruction 19
and the 4 to 0x200000 loading transition into the admitted set. Every async
loading service keeps its guard, so the first unqualified FELoadingToGame
request stops with its service number.

The loading scripts then push the original in-game overlays: navigation (30),
HUD (89), in-game text (90), goal (95), Mega Strike meter (100), PIP (101) and
super ability (102); their factory cases are admitted here. LoadingTask admits
the 0x200000 -> 2 hand-off and transitions between in-match task states (mask
0x2001B). FrontEnd::Update (admitted by 0615) pushes the original pause menu
(80) on Plus and the post-game results/statistics pages (91/92) at game over;
those cases are admitted too. Pause sub-pages (81-83, 104) and the
Strikers 101/Challenge pre-game pages (84, 103) keep their gates.

